[17.077742, "o", "Warning: running headless with --yolo / approval-mode=yolo and no sandbox. All tool calls (shell, write, edit) auto-execute at this process's privilege level. Configure tools.executionSandbox on Linux or a supported legacy sandbox via --sandbox / QWEN_SANDBOX, or set QWEN_CODE_SUPPRESS_YOLO_WARNING=1 to silence this notice.\r\n"]
[81.977192, "o", "Done. `/srv/shared` is configured and inheritance was verified on a disposable clone, leaving `/srv/shared` empty as required.\r\n\r\n## Final state\r\n\r\n```\r\ndrwxrws---+  root research  /srv/shared        # mode 2770, setgid\r\n\r\n# file: /srv/shared\r\n# owner: root\r\n# group: research\r\n# flags: -s-\r\nuser::rwx\r\nuser:alice:rwx\r\nuser:bob:rwx\r\ngroup::rwx\r\ngroup:research:rwx\r\nmask::rwx\r\nother::---\r\ndefault:user::rwx\r\ndefault:user:alice:rwx\r\ndefault:user:bob:rwx\r\ndefault:group::rwx\r\ndefault:group:research:rwx\r\ndefault:mask::rwx\r\ndefault:other::---\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Verification (run in `/tmp/aclclone` with identical ACLs, then deleted)\r\n\r\n| Check | Result |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| alice creates file → group `research`, ACLs inherited (`user:alice:rwx`, `user:bob:rwx`) | ✅ |\r\n| alice creates subdir → `drwxrws---+`, setgid + default ACLs inherited | ✅ |\r\n| File nested 2 levels deep still inherits alice/bob entries | ✅ |\r\n| bob reads alice's file | ✅ `hi` |\r\n| bob writes to alice's file / dir | ✅ |\r\n| `nobody` (non-research) lists dir | ❌ `Permission denied` (expected) |\r\n| `nobody` reads contents | ❌ `Permission denied` (expected) |\r\n| `/srv/shared` file count | `0` (untouched) |\r\n\r\n## Notes on how this satisfies the requirements\r\n\r\n- **Setgid (`2770`)** makes new entries inherit group `research`; the explicit `chgrp research` plus `drwxrws---+` confirms it.\r\n- **`mask::rwx` / `default:mask::rwx`** is the \"proper mask\" — without it the named user/group entries would be capped below full permissions.\r\n- **File mask is `rw-` by design.** A newly created regular file shows `mask::rw-` because the kernel limits inherited ACL mask to the creating mode (`0666`). Alice and bob still get full read/write access, which is what \"accessible by both users\" requires; directories correctly keep `mask::rwx` plus setgid for recursion.\r\n- **`other::---` on both access and default ACLs** blocks traversal/read for anyone outside `research`, even if a test creates a file with permissive `umask`.\r\n- Nothing was created inside `/srv/shared`, so the test phase starts from a clean directory.\r\n"]
